 # Decisions
 
 A decision is a question a worker cannot answer alone.
+
+## Shape
+
+Each decision offers **2 to 4 options**. Every option has a short `label`
+and a one-line `consequence` so the captain can choose without reading the
+whole task log. The worker marks one option as `recommended`.
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "d-17",
+  "question": "Drop support for Node 18?",
+  "options": [
+    { "label": "Drop it", "consequence": "CI matrix shrinks by a third" },
+    { "label": "Keep it", "consequence": "Polyfill stays until April" }
+  ],
+  "recommended": 0,
+  "state": "open",
+  "answer": null
+}
+```
+
+## Answering
+
+`POST /v1/decisions/{id}:answer` with `{"option": <index>}`.
+
+- Answers are final; a second answer returns `409`.
+- An index outside `options` returns `422`.
